# Deploy

GitHub is version control only. Never GitHub Pages, `actions/deploy-pages`, or
`withastro/action`. Never treat a merge to `main` or a green GitHub check as
published.

**Published** = a visitor can see the change at https://rtikhonov.com

## Live tree (read this first)

This `main` checkout is **not** production. Production is Cloudflare Worker
`rtikhonov`. Source:

- Folder: `rtikhonov.com/` (must contain `wrangler.jsonc`)
- Git line: `origin/cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting`
- Command: `cd rtikhonov.com && npm run deploy`

If this checkout has no `rtikhonov.com/wrangler.jsonc`:

```bash
git fetch origin cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting
git checkout -b cursor/<change>-433e origin/cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting
```

Edit `rtikhonov.com/src/`. Do not implement live changes in the root `src/`
on `main`.

## Auth (before any ship)

```bash
cd rtikhonov.com && npx wrangler whoami
```

Cloud Agents need `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` in the Cursor environment secrets.
If whoami fails: stop and ask for that token. Do not merge and say it is live.

## Ship

```bash
cd rtikhonov.com && npm run deploy
```

Then curl https://rtikhonov.com (no-cache) for the new string. Report the
Wrangler Version ID. Call it published only if the live page shows the change.
